es": ["Incumbent Lauren Boebert (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Lauren Boebert seeks another term in a district that leans Republican by about nine points, a structural advantage most race raters still treat as decisive. Cook and Inside Elections call the seat Solid Republican, several others rate it Likely or Lean Republican, and prediction markets give Republicans roughly a 72 percent chance of holding it.\n\nThe challenge is real, though. Eileen Laubacher has raised about $13 million to Boebert's $1.2 million and holds a large cash advantage for the final stretch, and the political environment favors Democrats this cycle. The only available polling, conducted by a Democratic sponsor in late September, showed Boebert ahead by just five points, and negative coverage has kept the incumbent on the defensive. The seat remains Republican-leaning, but not safely so.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1824, "margin": -5.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3343, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1945, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2743, "margin": -4.7}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2626, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.23, "margin": -4.7}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2582, "margin": -4.8}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2829, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2916, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2767, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3037, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.311, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.297, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2522, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2256, "margin": -4.7}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2601, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.2778, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.2282, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.1951, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem"